  "assessment_and_plan": "ASSESSMENT AND PLAN: Right elbow contusion due to a contusion from a lacrosse stick. Prescribed: Ibuprofen 800 mg twice daily, ice therapy three times a day for 20 minutes, rest from lacrosse for the next couple of weeks. Blood pressure: Continue on 20 mg lisinopril, diet compliant. Diabetes: Continue on 500 mg metformin, A1C test to check levels in the future."
}

{
  "subjective": "CHIEF COMPLAINT: Right ankle pain and swelling after falling on ice.\nHISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS: Gregory fell on icy ground and experienced ankle pain and swelling. He was able to walk a little bit better last night and today, but still limps. He has taken ibuprofen and the pain is somewhat relieved. He has not experienced any numbness in the foot.\nREVIEW OF SYSTEMS: No other complaints noted.",
