  "objective_results": "RESULTS: EKG: Normal. Blood pressure trend: Elevated. Hemoglobin A1c: Not provided. Blood pressure readings: Elevated trend. Chest pain: Unstable angina suspected. Chest pain: Refer to cardiology. Diabetes: Continue metformin. Eye exam: Ophthalmology appointment. High blood pressure: Hydrochlorothiazide prescribed. Blood pressure monitoring at home.",
  "assessment_and_plan": "ASSESSMENT AND PLAN: Unstable angina suspected due to chest pain, diabetes, and high blood pressure. Chest pain: Refer to cardiology. Diabetes: Continue metformin, eye exam, and hemoglobin A1c test. High blood pressure: Hydrochlorothiazide prescribed, blood pressure monitoring at home, and follow-up in two weeks. Chest pain: Aspirin and nitroglycerin prescribed for chest pain management. Blood pressure: Hydrochlorothiazide prescribed, blood pressure monitoring at home, and follow-up in two weeks. Side effects: Cross-reaction with sulfa medications. Follow-up in two weeks for blood pressure and diabetes management."
}

{
  "subjective": "CHIEF COMPLAINT: Back pain, radiating down left leg. HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS: The patient reports a sudden onset of low back pain after lifting a box of books a couple of weeks ago. The pain is described as achy and sharp, and has worsened, causing radiating pain down the left leg. The patient has tried ibuprofen and Tylenol, which sometimes help. The patient has a family history of back pain, with their father having similar issues. The patient is an Olympic weightlifter with a sedentary job and a history of playing soccer as a midfielder. REVIEW OF SYSTEMS: No loss of sensation, weakness, or bladder/bowel dysfunction noted.",
  "objective_exam": "PHYSICAL EXAMINATION: Vitals: Blood pressure 130/70 mmHg, respiratory rate 18 breaths/min, heart rate 78 beats/min, regular rhythm. Skin: No overlying redness or bruising. Musculoskeletal: Midline tenderness at the L4-L5 disk space with right-sided lumbar paravertebral tenderness. Flexion and extension movements are possible without pain. Supine straight leg test is positive.",
  "objective_results": "RESULTS: MRI shows disk desiccation, disk bulge, paracentral disk herniation resulting in moderate right neural foraminal stenosis. Neurological exam: Symmetrical patella and Achilles reflexes. No decreased sensation noted.",
